{"title":"Knit Hello, a Simple Typeface for Knitting","link":"https://kottke.org/25/10/knit-hello-a-simple-typeface-for-knitting","date":1759935643000,"content":"\n        <p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/knit-hello-01.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/knit-hello-01.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/knit-hello-01.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1300\" height=\"532\" alt=\"a knitted piece next to text that says 'it was made for beginners, knitters, and typographers who love type'\" /></p>\n\n<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/knit-hello-02.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/knit-hello-02.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/knit-hello-02.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1300\" height=\"905\" alt=\"a scarf with a bunch of knitted words for 'hello' in different languages\" /></p>\n\n<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/knit-hello-03.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/knit-hello-03.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/knit-hello-03.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1300\" height=\"867\" alt=\"a blue patterned scarf with the repeated letter A\" /></p>\n\n<p>Designer Rüdiger Schlömer has created a new typeface for beginning knitters called <a href=\"https://www.knithello.com/\">Knit Hello</a>.</p>\n\n<blockquote><p>Knit Hello is a typeface for hand knitting. It was made for beginners: knitters and typographers who love type.</p></blockquote>\n\n<p>You may remember Schlömer from his Futura-based <a href=\"https://kottke.org/23/04/knit-grotesk-a-typeface-for-hand-knitting\">Knit Grotesk</a>. And of course, the earliest bitmap letters weren’t found on a computer screen; blocky letters have been used in cross stitch and knitting for <a href=\"https://americanhistory.si.edu/collections/object-groups/american-samplers\">hundreds of years</a>. (via <a href=\"https://www.thisiscolossal.com/2025/10/knit-hello-typeknitting-rudiger-schlomer-digital-font-knitting-pattern/\">colossal</a>)</p>\n\n        \n\n         <p><strong>Tags:</strong> <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/design\">design</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/Rudiger%20Schlomer\">Rudiger Schlomer</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/typography\">typography</a></p>\n\n         <p>💬 <a href=\"https://kottke.org/25/10/knit-hello-a-simple-typeface-for-knitting\">Join the discussion on kottke.org</a> →</p>\n\n    ","author":"Jason Kottke","siteTitle":"Kottke","siteHash":"89a883271b4598f9b33ebe87be70d38557bcd266e68aee521a8f93622e0ab723","entryHash":"5245e4d0b445865498bc9373debbb9d267d3b856b30ae07b79e92c188bd1c803","category":"Sites"}